  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>The function \(f\) is given by \(f(x)=(x-2)(x+4)\). </para>
<para>Without using graphing technology, answer questions 1 – 4.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What are the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph representing \(f\)? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(x\)-intercepts for function \(f\): \((2,0)\) and \((-4,0)\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="e3dc9f2d-934a-463e-938f-92d2a57cd2a8" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3ef6b782-dbe3-4cae-a77c-9770e9a31299" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-1">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:<emphasis/></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -1</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9aa23552-aece-4c85-9209-34ffe324d66e" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-9">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:<emphasis/></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -9</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the \(y\)-intercept?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> The \(y\)-intercept is \((0,-8)\), because \((0-2)(0+4)=(-2)(4)=-8\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Sketch a graph that represents \(f\).</para>
    <para>Select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>The graph opens upward with vertex at \((-1,-9)\) and \(x\)-intercepts at \((2,0)\) and \((-4, 0)\).</para>
  <para><figure><media alt="Graph on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/881615b7474f3ba14c771ce12346fe82e703bc6d"/></media></figure></para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
